## File Change Summary

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/router/navigate.js` | Modify | `onRouteChanged` | Removed `next` parameter; replaced all `next(x)` / `next()` calls with `return x` / `return true` to use Vue Router 4's return-value guard pattern |
| `src/router/index.ts` | Modify | `router.beforeEach` | Switched from async callback with `next` to returning the promise from `onRouteChanged`, fixing the "next() called multiple times" / async warning |

### Why this fixes both issues

| Problem | Cause | Fix |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `/quick-chat` not rendering | `beforeEach` didn't `await` the async guard, so `next()` was called after the guard had already resolved without navigating | Guard now returns a `Promise` that Vue Router 4 **natively awaits** |
| `next()` warning | Vue Router warns when `next` is either not called or called after the microtask boundary in async guards | `next` is removed entirely; the return-value API has no such restriction |

